codex
The non-vacuity mutation built cleanly and failed for the expected unmet heap equality, so the reachability claim does constrain its formal result. However, the opposite-interpretation probe also built cleanly and proved the contract-violating result `[11, 1]` for input `[1, 11]` once the otherwise-unconstrained `sortKeyVS` was interpreted as reversal. That is the decisive soundness/adequacy failure I’m documenting in the final review.
Stage 5 found a decisive Gate A failure in the used opaque keyed-sort abstraction, with a concrete opposite-interpretation witness. Stage 6 confirmed the original formal result is non-vacuous but only constrains the opaque term.
  ✓ Read required Kit skill instructions and establish audit workspace
