  ✓ Stage 2: verify program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Stage 3: reconstruct definitions cleanly and rerun all positive proof claims
  ✓ Stage 4: audit claim adequacy and pinning to the real submitted program
  ✓ Stage 5: inventory and statically review every relevant K declaration and rule
  ✓ Stage 6: create and run a fresh meaningful false mutation
  ✓ Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and issue REVIEW.md verdict
